<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="skill">unarmed-combat</ansi> skill

The <ansi fg="skill">unarmed-combat</ansi> skill governs fighting with
fists, claws, and bare hands.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Attacks ━━━</ansi>

  - <ansi fg="stat">Both Hands:</ansi> Every empty hand attacks as a fist.
    Two arms = two fists. Six arms = six fists.
  - <ansi fg="stat">Fist/Claws Weapons:</ansi> These train unarmed-combat,
    not weapon-combat. Empty offhand still punches.
  - <ansi fg="stat">Mixed Setup:</ansi> Sword in one hand, empty offhand?
    The free hand punches too.
  - <ansi fg="stat">No Dual-Wield Penalty:</ansi> Fists, claws, and bare
    hands fight naturally with no accuracy loss.
  - <ansi fg="stat">Grapple-Friendly:</ansi> Fists and claws have very
    short reach. They stay fully effective in clinches and ground
    grapples where long weapons become awkward.
  - <ansi fg="stat">Grapple Drift:</ansi> <ansi fg="skill">unarmed-combat</ansi>
    is the primary skill that determines who wins each round of a
    grapple's drift toward advance, hold, reversal, or escape.
    See <ansi fg="command">help grapple</ansi> for the full picture.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Speed ━━━</ansi>

Unarmed fighters are faster than armed ones. The speed bonus
compensates for having dodge as the only defense.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Defense ━━━</ansi>

Unarmed-style fighters (bare hands, fists, claws) can only
<ansi fg="stat">dodge</ansi>. You cannot parry without a weapon or block
without a shield.

Dodging trains <ansi fg="skill">unarmed-combat</ansi> and
<ansi fg="stat">dexterity</ansi>.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Progression ━━━</ansi>

This skill improves through use:
  - Landing hits with fists or claws
  - Using <ansi fg="command">kick</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">trip</ansi>,
    and <ansi fg="command">grapple</ansi>
  - Dodging attacks
  - Each arm that hits progresses the skill independently

<ansi fg="magenta-bold">See also:</ansi> <ansi fg="command">help combat</ansi>,
  <ansi fg="command">help kick</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help trip</ansi>,
  <ansi fg="command">help grapple</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help submission</ansi>
